! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routine IBP54-IBP65, pp.38 and 59 (octal
! 004653.00-004676.00): four COUNT-IMMEDIATE steps that manufacture
! their own branch instructions.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  Measured, not guessed: nine index-arithmetic
! operations were shown unreachable by the whole suite in one combined
! injection, and after IBOX-4 closed KC and SR, seven remained.  This
! block uses C+I FOUR TIMES and SC FOUR TIMES -- two of the seven --
! plus LCI, LV, SV and V+.
!
! HOW IT CHECKS ITSELF, which is unlike anything else in the suite.
! There is no SERS.  Each step stores the COUNT to scratch, reads it
! back as a VALUE, adds a constant, and stores the result OVER a
! branch-to-self further down the block.  If the arithmetic is right
! the overwritten word becomes a branch to the next link; if it is
! wrong the word stays a branch to itself and THE MACHINE STOPS.
!
! THE ARITHMETIC, all four sums derived from the constants before this
! was ever run.  Three facts make it computable on paper:
!
!   * LCI and C+I take "bits 0-17 of the address part" (p.25) -- the
!     19-bit field's TOP 18 bits, not the raw field.
!   * SC writes {count(18), 7 zeros, 7 preserved} into a half-word and
!     LV reads its top 24 bits as the value, so the round trip through
!     ISTOY MULTIPLIES THE COUNT BY 64 -- it turns a count into the
!     word address of a bit address.
!   * COM04 is a VF whose 24-bit value is 0.04, so V+ adds 4, which
!     sets bits 19-23 of the result to 00100 -- the branch opcode.
!     The arithmetic manufactures an instruction, not just an address.
!
! With LCI giving count = 04667:
!
!   IBP55  C+I  3   count 04672   SV into IBP59 writes 4672.04 -> IBP61
!   IBP56  C+I  1   count 04673   SV into IBP61 writes 4673.04 -> IBP62
!   IBP57  C+I  2   count 04675   SV into IBP62 writes 4675.04 -> IBP64
!   IBP58  C+I -1   count 04674   SV into IBP64 writes 4674.04 -> IBP63
!
! giving IBP59 -> IBP61 -> IBP62 -> IBP64 -> IBP63 -> IBP65, exactly
! the chain the listing's own comments name.
!
! THE FOURTH STEP IS THE ONE WORTH HAVING.  Its immediate is
! (8)777777.0, whose top 18 bits are MINUS ONE in eighteen-bit two's
! complement, so the sequence is +3, +1, +2, -1 -- and the -1 is why
! the chain runs IBP64 -> IBP63, backwards, the only link that does.
! A count subtraction that silently did nothing would send it to
! IBP65's address instead and the machine would run on into data.
!
! IBP65's VF is MEANT to be executed: the listing annotates it
! "-NOP,-.32", so the chain ends by falling through it.

        SLC, (8)6105.0
ISTOY   DD(BU,64,8), 0
COM04   VF, 0.04

        SLC, (8)4653.0
! The listing writes these count immediates as ADDRESS EXPRESSIONS
! (LCI,$X1,IBP58+2.32 and C+I,$X1,3.0) but the field they encode is
! the WORD part, and this assembler wants the count value itself --
! the same spelling gap as SHF's shift count.  The model's own note
! on p.25 records the verified form: "LCI,$X1,4" prints 4.03 02.
! IBP58+2.32 is word 04667, so that is what is written here.
IBP54   LCI, $X1, (8)4667                    ! set up count (= IBP58+2.32)
IBP55   C+I, $X1, 3                          ! C+3.0
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
        SV, $X1, IBP59                       ! store for test
        NOP, 0.0
IBP56   C+I, $X1, 1                          ! C+1.0
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
        SV, $X1, IBP61                       ! store for test
        NOP, 0.0
IBP57   C+I, $X1, 2                          ! C+2.0
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
        SV, $X1, IBP62                       ! store for test
        NOP, 0.0
IBP58   C+I, $X1, (8)777777                  ! C-1.0
        SC, $X1, ISTOY
        LV, $X1, ISTOY
        V+, $X1, COM04
        SV, $X1, IBP64                       ! store for test
        NOP, 0.0
        NOP
IBP59   B, 0.0
        BD, $                                ! becomes a branch to IBP61 + BD,$
IBP60   BD, $
        BD, $
IBP61   B, $
        BD, $                                ! becomes a branch to IBP62 + BD,$
IBP62   B, $
        BD, $                                ! becomes a branch to IBP64 + BD,$
IBP63   NOP, -1
        BD, IBP65                            ! still NOP-1 + BD,IBP65
IBP64   B, $
        BD, $                                ! becomes a branch to IBP63 + BD,$
IBP65   VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBP54
